---
import RandomPicker from '../components/RandomPicker.astro';
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ToolSeoSections from '../components/ToolSeoSections.astro';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Random Picker — Pick a random item from a list | Bizzon"
  description="Free browser-based Random Picker by Bizzon. Paste a list and pick one or multiple random items locally in your browser."
  canonicalPath="/random-picker"
  heading="Random Picker"
  intro="Paste a list and pick a random item, winner, name, task, meal, or option. Choose one item, multiple items, or shuffle the whole list."
>
  <RandomPicker />
  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Pick one or many</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Choose one random item, draw several winners, allow duplicates when needed, or shuffle a full list into a random order.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Private by default</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Your list stays in your browser. Bizzon does not upload, save, or process your names, ideas, or choices on a server.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Useful for decisions</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Pick winners, chores, meals, tasks, teams, names, ideas, destinations, or anything else from a simple line-by-line list.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-blue-50 p-6 md:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Related tools</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-700">Need to generate a password? Try the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/password-generator">Password Generator</a>. Need to clean a messy copied list first? Use the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/text-cleaner">Text Cleaner</a>. Need counts? Open the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/character-counter">Character Counter</a>. Want every browser utility in one place? Browse <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/tools">all Bizzon tools</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm md:p-8" aria-labelledby="random-picker-ideas-heading">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-blue-700">Decision workflows</p>
    <h2 id="random-picker-ideas-heading" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">Random picker ideas for real lists</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-600">A random picker is most useful when the list is clear, the rule is agreed before the draw, and the result can be used immediately. These examples show practical ways to use Bizzon without accounts or spreadsheet setup.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Giveaway winner picker</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Paste eligible entries one per line, decide whether duplicate entries are allowed, then draw one or several winners. For public promotions, keep a separate record of the rules and eligibility list before using any random draw.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Classroom random name picker</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Use a list of student names for reading turns, presentation order, quiz teams, or classroom jobs. Shuffle mode is helpful when every name should appear once before the list resets.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Team decision and task rotation</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Pick a facilitator, first reviewer, standup order, chore owner, backlog item, or experiment idea. For recurring rotations, draw multiple items or shuffle the full list into a fair order.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Raffle list and lunch picker</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Choose a raffle ticket, restaurant, movie, game, travel idea, or lunch option when a group is stuck. Paste the options, remove anything unavailable, then pick once and move on.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50 p-6 md:p-8" aria-labelledby="random-picker-clean-input-heading">
    <h2 id="random-picker-clean-input-heading" class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Fair draws need clean input</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-700">Before a draw, make sure each list item is on its own line, remove blank rows, and normalize copied text. The <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/text-cleaner">Text Cleaner</a> can tidy names or entries copied from email, forms, documents, and chat exports. For a broader privacy-first workflow, read the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/private-browser-tools">Private Browser Tools</a> guide.</p>
  </section>

  <ToolSeoSections slug="random-picker" />
</ToolLayout>
